    '{"B":"Clarithromycin inhibits rather than induces CYP3A4, so statin levels rise, not fall.","C":"Protein-binding displacement does not explain this severe rhabdomyolysis.","D":"The myopathy is caused by statin accumulation, not an autoimmune process.","E":"Simvastatin is metabolized hepatically and does not inhibit renal clarithromycin clearance."}'::jsonb,
    'medium'
